       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered the order. Without a clinical reason, I can't place an order this far above the safe range.\n\nAt 6,400 mg/day, this is twice the 3,200 mg/day adult maximum, and each 1,600 mg dose is twice the 800 mg single-dose maximum. I don't know of any standard adult indication for ibuprofen at this dose four times a day. The likely harms are serious: GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and metabolic acidosis. Your confirming the order doesn't change those risks, and a dose like this is usually a typo or a mix-up between per-dose and total-daily amounts.\n\n**Ways forward:**\n1. **Give me the indication or protocol.** If this is part of a specific regimen, tell me what it is. I'll enter the order with a note documenting it and flag it for pharmacy verification.\n2. **Use a dose within the usual range.** For example, 800 mg PO three or four times daily (up to 3,200 mg/day), and I'll enter it right away.\n3. **Enter it yourself or through pharmacy.** You can override the limit directly in the order-entry system, which will document your override. Or you can discuss the order with the clinical pharmacist.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
